## Control {{controlId}}: Control and Monitor the Use of Voice over Internet Protocol (VoIP) Technologies

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization controls and monitors VoIP technologies within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through Microsoft Teams voice policies and cross-tenant communication restrictions documented in "Unified Communications Policy v1.0" maintained by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

Microsoft Teams is the sole authorized VoIP platform for the CUI environment. All voice communications are encrypted using SRTP (Secure Real-Time Transport Protocol) with FIPS 140-2 validated cryptographic modules within the GCC High boundary.

**Teams Voice Controls:**
- External calling restricted to authorized domains and phone numbers per Teams calling policies
- PSTN connectivity (if enabled) routed through Microsoft-managed GCC High infrastructure
- Call recording and voicemail transcription governed by compliance retention policies
- Guest access to Teams voice features restricted per external access settings

{{#if crossTenantPolicyConfigured}}
**Cross-Tenant Communication Restrictions:**
Cross-tenant access policies restrict Teams federation and voice communications to explicitly authorized partner organizations, preventing unauthorized VoIP connections to untrusted tenants.
{{/if}}

{{#if conditionalAccessActive}}
**Access Enforcement:**
Conditional Access policies require compliant device and MFA authentication before accessing Teams voice features, ensuring only authorized users on trusted devices participate in VoIP communications.
{{/if}}

**Operational Procedure:**
- **Action:** Review Teams voice policies, external access configurations, and cross-tenant calling restrictions
- **Frequency:** Quarterly policy review, continuous monitoring via call quality dashboard
- **Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- **Documentation:** Unified Communications Policy v1.0, Teams Voice Configuration Standard

**Review Frequency:** Quarterly by ISSO

**Verification Method:** Examine Teams voice policy configurations, external access settings, cross-tenant access policies, and call detail records.

